<Lecture
  chapterSlug="05-lists"
  lessonSlug="04-grade-report"
  hook="Chapter 5 capstone — pulls together lists, loops, conditionals, functions. Five functions, one assembler."
>
  <h2>The 5 functions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>average(scores)</code> — mean; guard for empty</li>
    <li><code>highest(scores)</code> — max; guard for empty</li>
    <li><code>pass_count(scores, threshold=60)</code> — count passing scores</li>
    <li><code>letter_grade(avg)</code> — Ch.2 elif chain</li>
    <li><code>report(name, scores)</code> — orchestrator, calls all four</li>
  </ul>

  <Callout tone="warning" title="🔒 no_paste mode is ON">
    <p>Graded homework. Type it. Tutor maxes at L2.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>The shape</h2>
  <CodePlayground
    caption="The orchestrator — see how it composes the helpers"
    code={`def average(scores):
    if not scores:
        return 0.0
    return sum(scores) / len(scores)

def highest(scores):
    if not scores:
        return 0
    return max(scores)

def pass_count(scores, threshold=60):
    return len([s for s in scores if s >= threshold])

def letter_grade(avg):
    if avg >= 90: return "A"
    elif avg >= 80: return "B"
    elif avg >= 70: return "C"
    elif avg >= 60: return "D"
    else: return "F"

def report(name, scores):
    avg = average(scores)
    return {
        "name": name,
        "average": round(avg, 2),
        "highest": highest(scores),
        "pass_count": pass_count(scores),
        "grade": letter_grade(avg),
    }

print(report("Ada Lovelace", [85, 92, 78, 95, 88]))
print(report("Edge Case", []))`}
  />

  <Callout tone="pitfall" title="Why guard against empty lists?">
    <p>
      <code>sum([]) / len([])</code> raises <code>ZeroDivisionError</code>.
      <code>max([])</code> raises <code>ValueError</code>. The test
      <code>test_average_empty</code> hands you an empty list explicitly —
      handle it with one line: <code>if not scores: return 0.0</code>.
    </p>
  </Callout>

  <h2>Acceptance criteria</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All 8 tests pass</li>
    <li><code>report</code> calls at least 3 of the 4 helpers</li>
    <li><code>average</code> survives empty input</li>
    <li>All average values rounded to 2 decimals</li>
  </ul>
</Lecture>
